From: Exequiel Echevarria <exemetal@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] hal: use strscpy for Linux 7.2+ string operations

Modern kernels strictly discourage strncpy in favor of strscpy to avoid
unterminated buffers and compiler fortification warnings.

---
 hal/hal_com_phycfg.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hal/hal_com_phycfg.c b/hal/hal_com_phycfg.c
index 81bca10..3729d10 100644
--- a/hal/hal_com_phycfg.c
+++ b/hal/hal_com_phycfg.c
@@ -17,6 +17,10 @@
 #include <drv_types.h>
 #include <hal_data.h>
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 2, 0)
+#define strncpy strscpy
+#endif
+
 #define PG_TXPWR_1PATH_BYTE_NUM_2G 18
 #define PG_TXPWR_BASE_BYTE_NUM_2G 11
-- 
